# What must never leave this machine.
#
# Without this file the Vercel CLI uploaded the whole working directory, which
# meant two things were shipped to a third party on every deploy:
#
#   server/.env            local configuration, including key slots
#   server/prisma/dev.db   the local SQLite database, with test students in it
#
# The .env one also broke the hosted deploy outright rather than just leaking:
# env.js loads it with dotenv, so a bundled .env set DATABASE_URL to
# "file:./dev.db" and shadowed the real Postgres connection the platform had
# already provided. The app then reported no database while sitting on one.
#
# A student's data living in a file on their own machine is the privacy promise
# this product makes. Uploading that file is the one thing that cannot happen.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Build output and caches — the host rebuilds these itself.
node_modules
web/dist
server/prisma/pg.prisma

# Local tooling
.git
.vscode
.idea
*.log
